{%- comment -%}
  Local hook (runs from the theme's bib layout, after it composes `entrytype`
  and before it joins that with the date into the `periodical` line).

  1. Invited talks and seminars are stored as @misc entries with the venue in
     `howpublished`. The theme only renders a venue for article/proceedings/
     thesis types, so build one here — without the "In " prefix that
     proceedings get, which reads wrong for a seminar. Re-append `location`
     and `additional_info`, because overwriting `entrytype` drops what the
     layout already added.

  2. `additional_info` is passed through `markdownify`, which returns the text
     wrapped in a paragraph and followed by a newline. Stripping the tags
     leaves that newline at the end of `entrytype`, and the layout then writes
     ", <date>" straight after it — rendering as "text , Aug 2026" with a space
     before the comma. Trim it. This applies to every entry type, so journal
     entries carrying a "(Top n% …)" note are fixed too.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% if entry.type == 'misc' and entry.howpublished %}
  {% capture entrytype %}<em>{{ entry.howpublished }}</em>{% endcapture %}
  {% if entry.location %}
    {% capture entrytype %}{{ entrytype }}, {{ entry.location }}{% endcapture %}
  {% endif %}
  {% if entry.additional_info %}
    {% capture entrytype %}{{ entrytype }}{{ entry.additional_info | markdownify | remove: '<p>' | remove: '</p>' }}{% endcapture %}
  {% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% assign entrytype = entrytype | strip %}
